feat(p2): settings.json `detail`: how much of a turn the chat shows, the rest on its wheels

A level from 1 to 4 (default 3, the chat as before), read live from settings.json for the owner:
1. only the answer and its results; the turn's thinking, texts and tool calls on one wheel per turn, its sheet
   listing thinking ("Thought") and texts ("Note") among the calls, each opening its words;
2. the agent's texts in the transcript too; thinking and calls on a wheel between them;
3. thinking too, collapsed to a line; only runs of tool calls on wheels;
4. thinking open in full and each tool call as its own row that opens its detail; no wheels.

At detail 1 the turn's last text becomes its answer only once the agent stopped: while it works a text may still
turn out to be a note, so it stays on the wheel and the answer fades in once, instead of showing and then jumping
back onto the wheel. Rebuilt runs keep their wheel when it shows the same (entries compared as steps or words).

fix(p2): type check of the TUI mark-read test

assert.equal(x, undefined) narrows x to undefined for the rest of the test;
check the call count instead.
